  "id": "Compound::DB04575 - Gene::2099",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Quinestrol and Esr1 through a series of molecular similarities and binding interactions. Quinestrol, which resembles Allylestrenol and Norgestimate, shares structural and functional similarities with these compounds, which in turn bind to Esr1. This implies that Quinestrol may act through a similar mechanism as these related compounds, potentially targeting the same receptor. The common ancestor relationships, such as Quinestrol and Allylestrenol both belonging to the Steroid class, further support a shared pharmacological profile. The evidence suggests that Quinestrol may act as a competitive inhibitor of Esr1, similar to how Norgestimate and Norelgestromin bind to the receptor. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Quinestrol in modulating estrogen receptor signaling, particularly through its structural resemblance to progestins and steroids.",
